      command_pane.hpp
      command_pane.cpp
      layout.hpp
      layout.cpp

    components/
      status_component.hpp
      status_component.cpp
      inventory_component.hpp
      inventory_component.cpp

  util/
    strings.hpp
    strings.cpp
    math.hpp
    math.cpp
```

### Dependency rule

```text
util/*               -> standard library only
ui/view_models.hpp   -> standard library + domain types
ui/theme.*           -> FTXUI DOM/screen style types
ui/panes/*           -> view_models + theme + FTXUI DOM
ui/components/*      -> panes + state + FTXUI component
main.cpp             -> components + app/screen loop
```

### Avoid circular dependencies with these constraints

1. `theme.hpp` must not include pane headers.
2. `view_models.hpp` must not include `main.cpp` concepts or component headers.
3. `panes/*.hpp` must not include `components/*.hpp`.
4. `components/*.hpp` may include pane headers, but pane headers must never include component headers.
5. Utility headers should not include FTXUI unless they are specifically UI utilities.
6. `main.cpp` should depend on everything; nothing should depend on `main.cpp`.

If a pane needs shared data, pass a struct:

```cpp
struct StatusPaneViewModel {
  std::string title;
  int health;
  int max_health;
  bool focused;
};

ftxui::Element RenderStatusPane(const StatusPaneViewModel&);
```

Do not let panes reach into globals:

```cpp
// Avoid:
ftxui::Element RenderStatusPane(); // secretly reads global AppState
```

